# Self legacy verification

User-facing checks use Self Pass (`@selfxyz/qrcode` and `SelfBackendVerifier`). Do not call `sessions.create`.

A check is finished in either of these ways:

- Self feedback: the QR wrapper `onSuccess` when the relayer reports `proof_verified`.
- The legacy webhook: Self's relayer POSTs the proof to `https://devcity.fun/api/webhooks/self`. Mark the account only after `SelfBackendVerifier` accepts it.

The deeplink only brings the person back. The Verified tick comes from the webhook result. Keep a pending check so a return without the deeplink still looks up that result. Enterprise signed webhooks stay a fallback when `svix-signature` is present.

A person verifies once. If `identityVerifiedAt` is already set, do not start another Self check and do not replace the stored time or document. A repeat proof for that same account is a success so Self can finish. A document already stored on a different account stays rejected.
